## Modality Assessment

> **REQUIRED for non-trivial design or bounded documentation plans.** Classify
> each meaningful part before choosing a planning protocol.

| Part | Mode | Why | Planning Treatment |
|------|------|-----|--------------------|
| `known-doc-contract` | Deductive / plan-first | The authoritative source and pass/fail checks are knowable. | Specify docs, links, validation commands, and acceptance criteria. |
| `unknown-reader-need` | Exploratory / ladder | The useful shape must be learned from review, navigation, or usage. | Build the cheapest doc/view instrument, define the readout, and preserve step-down to concrete examples. |
| `mixed-doc-surface` | Hybrid | Some policy is fixed, but organization or emphasis must be learned. | Gate the fixed policy; instrument the uncertain surface until it can be promoted. |

**Exploratory readout:** What observable signal will end, redirect, or promote
the exploration?

**Step-down path:** How will a failing aggregate, metric, or review signal lead
back to the concrete docs or examples that explain it?

